<https://ontology.surveillancegraph.org/schema/GeometryKind> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The geometry shape kind a record declares for its subject (§19, SIG-GEO-003): the asset model MUST NOT assume a point. A record whose publisher's geometry is a zone or programme area declares `area` — automated-traffic-enforcement zones and published camera programme areas are areas, never device points — and a route-shaped record declares `line`. The `geometry_kind` predicate (ontology/vocab/predicates.yaml) carries this vocabulary's member on the claim surface; an area-shaped record MUST NOT be flattened to a device point." .
